      "text": "Consider a cache, which requires 2 clock cycles. If there is a cache miss, it will stall the processor for an additional 5 clock cycles. Then what will be the hit rate to achieve an average memory access of 3 clock cycles?",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "80%"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "85%"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "90%"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "95%"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "A",
      "correctText": "80%",
      "explanation": "Cache hit requires 2 clock cycles.\nCache miss requires 7 clock cycles.\nAverage memory access requires 3 clock cycles.\nLet hit rate is x, then 3 = x * 2 + (1 – x)7\n⇒ 3 = 2x + 7 – 7x\n⇒ 5x = 4\n⇒ x = \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\)×100 = 80%                                  Choice (A)",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
